{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":42995,"name":"Fridolín Pokorný","username":"fridex","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/fridex/{size}/11877_2.png","created_at":"2021-12-03T10:48:36.295Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi all,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003erecently we had a discussion about \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/thoth-station/micropipenv/issues/206\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003epossible reports created by pip\u003c/a\u003e that would be optionally produced when pip installs software.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConsider an example use case, when one installs packages into a containerized environment. The container image is shipped and one can introspect what packages are installed by issuing \u003ccode\u003epip list\u003c/code\u003e. Mind that the listing created by \u003ccode\u003epip list\u003c/code\u003e does not capture the index URL from where pip installed software. Also, information on artifact level (which wheel build was matching and used) is not captured in this report. Could pip eventually support easy to read reports created optionally - something like \u003ccode\u003epip install flask --report pip_install_report.json\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI would like to ask if the packaging community would be interested in such a feature. I haven’t found any way how to do such reporting with a recent pip version (without increasing verbosity of pip logs, which are essentially unstructured). Sorry if I missed anything.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks in advance for any response.\u003cbr\u003e\nFridolin\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2021-12-03T10:48:36.295Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1890,"reads":108,"readers_count":107,"score":9456.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":12316,"topic_slug":"pip-installation-reports","display_username":"Fridolín Pokorný","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/thoth-station/micropipenv/issues/206","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Create report containing information about packages installed · Issue #206 · thoth-station/micropipenv · GitHub","clicks":12},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-710-recording-the-provenance-of-installed-packages/25428","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"PEP 710 - Recording the provenance of installed packages","clicks":2},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/draft-pep-recording-provenance-of-installed-packages/24838","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Draft PEP: Recording provenance of installed packages","clicks":0},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/pre-pep-recording-provenance-of-installed-packages/23340","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Pre-PEP: Recording provenance of installed packages","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":1788,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pip-installation-reports/12316/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":42998,"name":"Paul Moore","username":"pf_moore","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/pf_moore/{size}/35_2.png","created_at":"2021-12-03T11:27:50.707Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThis should probably just be raised on the pip tracker. I’d personally be cautious about how we did this, as there’s a risk we burden pip with a big maintenance overhead, generating reports for all sorts of use cases. But adding an option to the install command to dump a bunch of extra raw data to a file, for 3rd party reporting, would be a reasonable feature to request.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2021-12-03T11:27:50.707Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":99,"readers_count":98,"score":19.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":12316,"topic_slug":"pip-installation-reports","display_username":"Paul Moore","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":35,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pip-installation-reports/12316/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":43000,"name":"Dustin Ingram","username":"dustin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/dustin/{size}/149_2.png","created_at":"2021-12-03T12:23:41.175Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eInstead of pip producing a multitude of reports upon request, perhaps it be better for pip to just begin storing the necessary metadata for these reports alongside an installation, so any third-party tool could generate any format of report, without needing to execute pip itself?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor example, this could eventually allow for a report could be generated from the static filesystem of a container image with Python packages installed, without needing to run the image.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2021-12-03T12:23:41.175Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":93,"readers_count":92,"score":43.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":12316,"topic_slug":"pip-installation-reports","display_username":"Dustin Ingram","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":120,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pip-installation-reports/12316/3","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":43002,"name":"Paul Moore","username":"pf_moore","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/pf_moore/{size}/35_2.png","created_at":"2021-12-03T13:47:41.069Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eYes, that would be probably be better (if only because it avoids the possibility that someone loses the file from the \u003ccode\u003epip install\u003c/code\u003e invocation \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/apple/wink.png?v=10\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"\u003e). Doing that \u003cem\u003eshould\u003c/em\u003e be raised here, though, as it would need a packaging PEP to define new installation metadata.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2021-12-03T13:47:41.069Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":3,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":92,"readers_count":91,"score":38.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":12316,"topic_slug":"pip-installation-reports","display_username":"Paul Moore","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"reply_to_user":{"id":120,"username":"dustin","name":"Dustin Ingram","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/dustin/{size}/149_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":35,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pip-installation-reports/12316/4","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":43004,"name":"Fridolín Pokorný","username":"fridex","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/fridex/{size}/11877_2.png","created_at":"2021-12-03T14:33:41.230Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eOK, sounds reasonable. Thanks for the replies and discussion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo clarify the effort, the goal here would be to eventually extend \u003ccode\u003epip list\u003c/code\u003e (or something similar) and provide an option to list more metadata kept for each installation. Eventually, something like \u003ccode\u003epip list --full\u003c/code\u003e - the listing could report package name, package version, index URL, used artifact, hash at first and have the solution extensible enough for future extensions, such as adding information about the installation of signed packages and so. The implementation could integrate with other \u003ccode\u003epip list\u003c/code\u003e options, such as \u003ccode\u003epip list --full --user --pre --format json\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt might be worth clarifying if the implementation will use a single “database” to store, associate and maintain such metadata (a single consistent file) or keep metadata spread per installation. I’m not that familiar with pip internals that much and this will probably indeed require a proper design proposal. The former probably fits to Dustin’s “obtain metadata without running the image” more.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2021-12-03T14:33:41.230Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":88,"readers_count":87,"score":42.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":12316,"topic_slug":"pip-installation-reports","display_username":"Fridolín Pokorný","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":1788,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pip-installation-reports/12316/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":43005,"name":"Paul Moore","username":"pf_moore","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/pf_moore/{size}/35_2.png","created_at":"2021-12-03T14:47:34.489Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"fridex\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"12316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/fridex/48/11877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e fridex:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo clarify the effort, the goal here would be to eventually extend \u003ccode\u003epip list\u003c/code\u003e (or something similar) and provide an option to list more metadata kept for each installation\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI would be against having the reporting itself in pip. I’m fine with the Python packaging tools recording the information needed to report on (I prefer \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/dustin\"\u003e@dustin\u003c/a\u003e’s suggestion of making that standard metadata), but I’d want any reporting to be handled by a dedicated tool, rather than making it part of pip. After all, the whole point of having packaging standards is so that we \u003cem\u003edon’t\u003c/em\u003e have to bundle everything into pip.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"fridex\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"12316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/fridex/48/11877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e fridex:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt might be worth clarifying if the implementation will use a single “database” to store, associate and maintain such metadata (a single consistent file) or keep metadata spread per installation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt would be stored with the installation, in the \u003ccode\u003e.dist-info\u003c/code\u003e directory. \u003ca href=\"https://packaging.python.org/specifications/recording-installed-packages/\"\u003eThis\u003c/a\u003e is the relevant standard you would be looking to extend.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2021-12-03T14:47:34.489Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":83,"readers_count":82,"score":51.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":12316,"topic_slug":"pip-installation-reports","display_username":"Paul Moore","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://packaging.python.org/specifications/recording-installed-packages/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Recording installed projects — Python Packaging User Guide","clicks":3}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":35,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pip-installation-reports/12316/6","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":43006,"name":"Dustin Ingram","username":"dustin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/dustin/{size}/149_2.png","created_at":"2021-12-03T15:01:54.834Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"pf_moore\" data-post=\"6\" data-topic=\"12316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/pf_moore/48/35_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e pf_moore:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’d want any reporting to be handled by a dedicated tool, rather than making it part of pip\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFull disclosure, I’m mostly thinking about this in the context of the recently-announced \u003ca href=\"https://pypi.org/project/pip-audit/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003epip-audit\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e tool, which already has support for generating \u003ca href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_bill_of_materials\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eSBOMs\u003c/a\u003e, and is planning to add \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/trailofbits/pip-audit/issues/69\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003esupport for auditing container images\u003c/a\u003e. I created \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/trailofbits/pip-audit/issues/170\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eDetailed installation reports · Issue #170 · pypa/pip-audit · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e to track this feature request there.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2021-12-03T15:39:47.259Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":80,"readers_count":79,"score":46.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":12316,"topic_slug":"pip-installation-reports","display_username":"Dustin Ingram","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/trailofbits/pip-audit/issues/170","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Detailed installation reports · Issue #170 · trailofbits/pip-audit · GitHub","clicks":6},{"url":"https://pypi.org/project/pip-audit/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"pip-audit · PyPI","clicks":4},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_bill_of_materials","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Software bill of materials - Wikipedia","clicks":3},{"url":"https://github.com/trailofbits/pip-audit/issues/69","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Support auditing container images · Issue #69 · trailofbits/pip-audit · GitHub","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":120,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pip-installation-reports/12316/7","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":43023,"name":"Brett Cannon","username":"brettcannon","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/brettcannon/{size}/34895_2.png","created_at":"2021-12-03T20:53:16.501Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"fridex\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"12316\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/fridex/48/11877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e fridex:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ethe listing could report package name, package version, index URL, used artifact, hash at first\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFYI this is all covered by PEP 665 if you record the wheel that gets installed (not sure if you want to record the sdist that a wheel may have been built from?), so if this information is recorded it could be used to create a lock file from what’s been installed so others can reproduce the environment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe key things in that list that aren’t covered in the core metadata are:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIndex URL\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe used artifact\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHash of the used artifact\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI guess this is sort of the index-installed equivalent of \u003ca href=\"https://packaging.python.org/specifications/direct-url/#direct-url\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eRecording the Direct URL Origin of installed distributions - Python Packaging User Guide\u003c/a\u003e?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2021-12-03T20:53:16.501Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":4,"reads":78,"readers_count":77,"score":70.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":12316,"topic_slug":"pip-installation-reports","display_username":"Brett Cannon","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"packaging-council","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/3X/0/5/05b580b0d5d0ba0258ddcb3685ca7006fcd0f01b.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":48,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://packaging.python.org/specifications/direct-url/#direct-url","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Recording the Direct URL Origin of installed distributions — Python Packaging User Guide","clicks":3}],"read":true,"user_title":"Packaging Council Member","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":36,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pip-installation-reports/12316/8","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":75638,"name":"Fridolín Pokorný","username":"fridex","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/fridex/{size}/11877_2.png","created_at":"2022-11-24T07:36:48.976Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eWe are evaluating a possibility to work on this and invest some time to deliver this feature. \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/brettcannon\"\u003e@brettcannon\u003c/a\u003e, and others, do you see any dependency here with respect to the lockfile related work we should consider?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2022-11-24T07:36:48.976Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":8,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":6,"reads":69,"readers_count":68,"score":53.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":12316,"topic_slug":"pip-installation-reports","display_username":"Fridolín Pokorný","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":36,"username":"brettcannon","name":"Brett Cannon","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/brettcannon/{size}/34895_2.png"},"book